 "designers": ["Lars Bak", "Kasper Lund", "Gilad Bracha"],
 "summary": "Client-optimized, class-based, garbage-collected language from Google, compiled ahead-of-time to native code, JIT-compiled in its VM for development, and compiled to JavaScript and WebAssembly; it is the language of the Flutter UI framework. Dart 2 made the type system sound, Dart 2.12 added sound null safety, and Dart 3 added records, patterns and class modifiers.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": ["vendor-specification", "consortium-standard", "reference-implementation"],
 "standards": ["ECMA-408 (Dart 1.x, 4th edition 2015)", "Dart Programming Language Specification (draft, 2.x/3.x)"],
 "file_extensions": [".dart", ".dill"],
 "homepage": "https://dart.dev/",
 "influenced_by": ["java", "javascript", "smalltalk", "strongtalk", "csharp", "erlang", "c"],
 "related": [{"id": "javascript", "relation": "compiles-to"}, {"id": "webassembly", "relation": "compiles-to"}, {"id": "java", "relation": "family"}, {"id": "kotlin", "relation": "family"}],
 "level_notes": {"0": "dart-lang/sdk is the single reference implementation: the shared front end (_fe_analyzer_shared, front_end) produces Kernel IR consumed by the VM (runtime/vm, JIT + AOT), dart2js, the dev compiler (DDC) and dart2wasm; the analyzer is a second front end used by IDEs. co19 is the language conformance suite.", "1": "Dart 1 was standardised as ECMA-408 (last edition 2015, now obsolete). The current specification is a LaTeX draft (dartLangSpec.tex, built as DartLangSpecDraft.pdf) that lags the language; new features are defined first by feature specifications in dart-lang/language/accepted, which are normative until folded into the spec. Spec deep links below are PDF page links into the draft and may shift when it is rebuilt.", "2": "dart.dev/language is the official language tour (per-concept pages); Effective Dart is the official style/usage guide. 'Understanding null safety' (Nystrom) is the main design explainer."},
